1
00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:03,720
You like it rough, don't you?

2
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:10,420
Ryo-san, we know what you're going to say.
Give up and come out!

3
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:15,460
You're paying for six months of Kamesuke's debts,
starting today.

4
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:17,320
This comes to 55,000 yen in total.

5
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:18,600
Pay for the three of ours too.

6
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:23,940
Is it right to lie to a police officer?
Open up, Ryotsu!

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,420
We're not leaving until
you pay us today too.

8
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:29,380
Come out already.

9
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:32,720
Come out!

10
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:40,060
Thirty seconds left

11
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:43,200
Looks like this one's no good.

12
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:44,480
In that case,

13
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:54,280
Five seconds left.

14
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:54,960
4

15
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:55,720
3

16
00:00:56,250 --> 00:00:56,620
2

17
00:00:57,090 --> 00:00:57,460
1

18
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:05,660
Now then, Mr. Ryotsu,

19
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:06,600
boss,

20
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:08,840
how much debt have you racked up, anyway?

21
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:12,140
It's nothing much, just about 180,000 yen.

22
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:14,140
That's the same as my take-home pay.

23
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:15,960
Don't be so timid about it.

24
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:18,740
It's hard to choose, isn't it?

25
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:20,680
Wouldn't Hokkaido be nice?

26
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,880
They say the autumn leaves
have already started, too.

27
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:24,820
Okinawa is hard to pass up, too.

28
00:01:24,820 --> 00:01:26,140
And you can go scuba diving there.

29
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:27,660
I said Hokkaido!

30
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:29,120
Okinawa is better.

31
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:30,000
Hokkaido?

32
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:32,820
Hokkaido, Hokkaido, Hokkaido

33
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:34,840
Okinawa, Okinawa, Okinawa, Okinawa

34
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:35,920
Hmm

35
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:38,080
Now, now, you two.

36
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:40,980
Yo!

37
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:42,740
Hey, what's going on?

38
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:46,700
We were actually talking about
the police box's staff trip.

39
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:48,860
So where are we going, anyway?

40
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:50,940
Ryo-chan, Hokkaido would be nice, right?

41
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:52,920
There's all-you-can-eat autumn delicacies!

42
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:54,940
Senpai,
Okinawa is the obvious choice, right?

43
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:56,820
It's full of resort vibes!

44
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:59,060
Hokkaido or Okinawa...

45
00:01:59,060 --> 00:02:00,560
Neither really does it for me.

46
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:03,100
If we're going, I'd rather go abroad.

47
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:06,160
Like Hawaii,
or Guam to get that tropical feel.

48
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:09,880
That's impossible.
The budget won't allow it.

49
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:10,880
How much is it?

50
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:12,960
It's 48,000 yen per person.

51
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:14,800
Even I, after the last trip,

52
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:17,700
said we'd go all out next time,
saving from our meager salaries,

53
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:21,180
we've been diligently putting away
2,000 yen a month for two years.

54
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:24,980
For reference, Ryo-chan has only
three months' worth saved up.

55
00:02:24,980 --> 00:02:25,600
Shut up.

56
00:02:26,340 --> 00:02:28,220
Yeah, with that much, it's more than enough.

57
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:31,800
I'll take you on an overseas trip,

58
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:39,180
and I'll skim off the travel money nicely.

59
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:42,040
That'll go toward paying off my debts.

60
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:44,580
Aren't I just brilliant?

61
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:54,980
Sincere Travel Agency

62
00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:56,380
Kind of a suspicious name.

63
00:02:57,040 --> 00:03:00,500
Wasn't this the spot where that
crooked real estate agency used to be?

64
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:02,200
Well, whatever.

65
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:05,200
Only one contract this month so far

66
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:08,560
I've got to do something,
or I'll be buried in debt.

67
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:09,120
Listen!

68
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:13,580
Why is that guy here again?

69
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:15,060
Juice!

70
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:16,660
Welcome!

71
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:19,940
Welcome to the Sincerity-First
Sincere Travel Agency.

72
00:03:19,940 --> 00:03:22,600
Long time no see,
you crooked real estate swindler.

73
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:24,300
Crooked? How rude.

74
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:27,320
What are you doing at a travel agency?

75
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:30,320
Well, the real estate industry
is in an ice age right now.

76
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:33,100
I switched over to an
overseas travel agency.

77
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:36,100
You're probably up to your old scams again.

78
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:38,060
I'm not lying about that, not one bit.

79
00:03:38,420 --> 00:03:40,320
Ever since then,
I've turned over a new leaf.

80
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,140
Sincerity is my only way.

81
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:45,840
I've been working hard,
giving it my all at my job.

82
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:49,020
Sincerity above all, right?

83
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:50,060
Y-yes.

84
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:50,140
Hey!

85
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:54,360
Actually, we want to take a company trip,
since this is where we all started.

86
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:57,580
I-I see, sir.
And where were you thinking of going?

87
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:01,600
Three nights, four days, somewhere like Guam,
Saipan, or another tropical island would be nice.

88
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:04,100
Sir, you're a very lucky customer.

89
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:08,480
We just received information
on a super-cheap Guam tour!

90
00:04:09,054 --> 00:04:12,500
How about this one?
Three nights, four days, sixty thousand yen.

91
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:15,420
The hotel is top-class too,
so it's a real bargain.

92
00:04:16,180 --> 00:04:17,480
So, how are we getting there?

93
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:18,020
Gulp!

94
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:20,980
W-well, we're flying, obviously.

95
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:22,020
Gulp!

96
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:24,560
What's this written in small print?

97
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:25,480
Gulp, gulp!

98
00:04:26,180 --> 00:04:28,120
Meeting point: Guam Airport?

99
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:30,940
So that means the plane
fare is extra, right?!

100
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:35,020
Where exactly did you turn over a new leaf

101
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:37,840
You haven't changed a bit from the old days.
Same old tricks.

102
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:42,400
I'm terribly sorry.

103
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:45,340
Stop being so pushy. No way, no way.

104
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:47,720
This is our super-special top-deal tour!

105
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:50,180
Airfare is included, too.

106
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:52,360
Three nights, four days in Saipan,
sixty thousand yen.

107
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:54,240
So what about the hotel?

108
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:57,440
It's called Honjama Hotel,
and it's quite a decent hotel.

109
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:58,960
Honjama Hotel

110
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:00,840
Wait, this sign...

111
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:01,300
*twitch*

112
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:04,080
The sign says "Honjama Hotel," though.

113
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:07,160
Did I mishear that?

114
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,960
Could you tell me the hotel
we'd be staying at again?

115
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:11,620
Honjama Hotel.

116
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:13,520
Could you point to it somewhere?

117
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:16,580
This one?

118
00:05:17,540 --> 00:05:19,780
Such an unnatural way of pointing.

119
00:05:19,780 --> 00:05:20,620
*stiffen*

120
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:21,260
and...

121
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:22,780
What is this?!

122
00:05:24,980 --> 00:05:31,080
This shabby hotel behind the luxurious Honjama Hotel is also called Honjama Hotel,
isn't it!

123
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,280
Th-that's, well...

124
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:35,340
I-I stand corrected!

125
00:05:35,740 --> 00:05:38,820
We see right through your tricks,
Koshitora-chan!

126
00:05:39,020 --> 00:05:41,820
Hey, you! Stop peddling junk
and give us a proper tour already!

127
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:43,940
Any southern island is fine with me,

128
00:05:43,940 --> 00:05:46,160
but the hotel and the food better be decent.

129
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:48,800
Of course, it should be a
proper trip where we fly there.

130
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:50,020
Yes, understood.

131
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:51,880
We'll arrange it for you.

132
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:54,260
You understand? That's good.

133
00:05:54,260 --> 00:05:55,640
So, about the price.

134
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:58,340
Since it's a group trip for five,
give us the group discount,

135
00:05:58,340 --> 00:06:00,260
so let's say 30,000 yen per person.

136
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:01,260
30,000 yen?

137
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:03,040
Yes, 30,000 yen.

138
00:06:03,040 --> 00:06:04,800
That's absurd!

139
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:07,400
Nowadays, even a domestic trip
is impossible for 30,000 yen.

140
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,920
So that's how it is?

141
00:06:11,820 --> 00:06:15,413
Attention, passersby!
This honest travel agency

142
00:06:15,463 --> 00:06:18,340
runs a business that is strictly prohibited.

143
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,460
Everyone, let's be careful
not to have a single blemish.

144
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:22,380
Alright, alright. Please stop.

145
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:26,340
Let's settle on four.

146
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:31,740
Attention, passersby!
This honest travel agency

147
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:35,460
will somehow manage to do it for 30,000 yen.

148
00:06:35,940 --> 00:06:39,200
Well, why didn't you just
say that from the start?

149
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:44,060
Hey! Keep it a secret from everyone
that this trip costs 30,000.

150
00:06:44,060 --> 00:06:45,300
Why is that?

151
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:47,720
Just because. Understood?

152
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:48,440
Y-yes.

153
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:52,560
You know what'll happen
if you spill it, right?

154
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:54,280
Yes, I understand.

155
00:06:55,340 --> 00:06:57,440
Hmm

156
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:58,840
Hehehehehe.

157
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:02,500
If we each saved 18,000 yen,
that's 90,000 yen for five of us.

158
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:05,120
My debt's 180,000, so we're halfway there.

159
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,740
Wait, a company trip?

160
00:07:08,020 --> 00:07:08,740
Hey, want to come along?

161
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:12,600
But the Hakubai unit has one next month too,
so I'm -

162
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:15,460
You're just going to some rundown hot spring,
aren't you?

163
00:07:15,460 --> 00:07:17,360
Our trip is amazing.

164
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:20,140
It's a super deluxe, three-night,
four-day trip to a southern island.

165
00:07:20,140 --> 00:07:22,520
Overseas? That's incredible.

166
00:07:23,060 --> 00:07:24,780
Southern islands are great.

167
00:07:24,780 --> 00:07:28,260
You'd be out there riding jet skis

168
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:31,040
and getting swarmed by
blonde bikini babes, I bet.

169
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,580
You are exciting boy!

170
00:07:50,660 --> 00:07:53,240
Touch me and you'll get burned!

171
00:07:56,960 --> 00:08:00,440
That sounds great, senpai!

172
00:08:00,780 --> 00:08:04,260
But it's not just one night in Atami,
so the cost is high, you know.

173
00:08:04,260 --> 00:08:05,640
How much is it?

174
00:08:05,640 --> 00:08:10,180
Let's see, the remaining 90,000 yen of
debt plus the actual cost of 30,000 yen.

175
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:14,120
Plus the 6,000 yen for three months of my savings payments,
added in.

176
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:16,900
That comes to about 126,000 yen in total.

177
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:20,040
126,000 yen... that's a bit much.

178
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:22,080
Oh well, that's too bad.

179
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:25,940
Since we're close,
I specially invited you alone, you know.

180
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:28,780
No jet bikes, and no blond hair either.

181
00:08:28,780 --> 00:08:31,680
Understood, I'll cancel my commuter
pass and get the money ready.

182
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:34,800
Great! Now my debts are wiped out!

183
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:41,180
Is he really reliable enough?

184
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:43,620
After what happened to us the other day,

185
00:08:43,620 --> 00:08:44,640
that's right.

186
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:45,580
It's fine, it's fine.

187
00:08:45,980 --> 00:08:46,700
Really?

188
00:08:46,700 --> 00:08:49,220
Honestly, even going on a trip with you

189
00:08:49,220 --> 00:08:51,580
after what happened last time,
I'm still fed up with it.

190
00:08:51,580 --> 00:08:52,680
That's uncalled for.

191
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:56,500
Thanks to me, we can travel to
a southern island at that price,

192
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:57,820
yet all you do is complain.

193
00:08:57,820 --> 00:09:00,480
I think I deserve more gratitude.

194
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:02,160
Th-that's right, Chief.

195
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:04,380
Th-that's true, of course.

196
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:07,460
Well, as long as you understand.

197
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:09,300
What are you whispering about?

198
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:11,040
Well, let's go check in for the flight.

199
00:09:11,540 --> 00:09:12,160
Yeah, let's.

200
00:09:12,420 --> 00:09:13,860
Hey, Ceiling-man, you'd better handle it.

201
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:14,580
Y-yes.

202
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:16,220
Now, everyone, this way please.

203
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:23,420
Have a pleasant trip.

204
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:24,480
Thanks.

205
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:27,460
Okay, that's all for here.

206
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:28,680
W-why is that?

207
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:30,720
From here on, you'll be seated separately.

208
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:31,620
Separate seats?

209
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:48,879
By the way, you said only
Ryozu is being seated separately,

210
00:09:48,929 --> 00:09:51,660
you don't mean he's in first class, do you?

211
00:09:51,820 --> 00:09:55,600
No, no, no. That gentleman is...

212
00:09:57,060 --> 00:09:59,240
Damn it! Here again?!

213
00:10:20,700 --> 00:10:23,360
Here, you'll be transferring
to that seaplane over there.

214
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:25,480
A seaplane?

215
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:26,600
It's kind of lovely, isn't it?

216
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:30,500
Please watch your step as you walk.

217
00:10:34,420 --> 00:10:35,220
That's all.

218
00:10:36,160 --> 00:10:37,480
What's the meaning of this?

219
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:41,220
Since we could only secure
five seats in the cabin,

220
00:10:41,220 --> 00:10:42,640
the passengers will be outside.

221
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:46,000
W-what do you mean, outside?!

222
00:10:46,540 --> 00:10:49,480
Please hold on to whichever you like,
the wings or the tail.

223
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:53,920
What?! Then you be the one outside!
We're customers, customers!

224
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:56,380
I-I'm sorry, but, well, sir, ma'am!

225
00:10:56,500 --> 00:10:57,620
Hey, idiot!

226
00:10:57,680 --> 00:11:01,000
Hey, Ryotsu! What's all the fuss about?
They say we're taking off!

227
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:03,160
Nah, there's no fuss at all!

228
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:09,720
If you don't hurry, you'll miss the flight!

229
00:11:10,660 --> 00:11:11,300
What?!

230
00:11:14,740 --> 00:11:15,980
Don't take off!

231
00:11:17,920 --> 00:11:18,720
Idiot!

232
00:11:20,660 --> 00:11:21,520
Yaaah!

233
00:11:34,180 --> 00:11:37,100
The pilot is Japanese?

234
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:41,140
You wouldn't think it, but I used to fly
a Zero for the old Imperial Japanese Army.

235
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:47,520
And since there are hardly any Japanese passengers,
I'll give you all a special service!

236
00:11:47,580 --> 00:11:48,300
Service?

237
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:50,440
What? You'll love it, I tell you!

238
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:51,460
Why, why?!

239
00:11:51,940 --> 00:11:52,960
Yahoo!

240
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:55,220
Phew, give me a break!

241
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:04,200
Oh crap!

242
00:12:08,300 --> 00:12:09,020
Go, go!

243
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:09,700
Whoa!

244
00:12:12,820 --> 00:12:13,600
Did you enjoy that?!

245
00:12:17,260 --> 00:12:18,920
The senior officer fell off.

246
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:20,920
What, don't worry about him.

247
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:22,440
He'll probably swim after us.

248
00:12:31,460 --> 00:12:32,740
Thank you for your hard work.

249
00:12:33,220 --> 00:12:35,800
This is our destination, Ottodokkoi Island.

250
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:38,240
Shall we assign the rooms first?

251
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:39,980
Or would you like to eat first?

252
00:12:39,980 --> 00:12:40,700
Food, food!

253
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:41,000
Yay!

254
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:47,280
Lunch is a buffet at the hotel.

255
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:50,760
Why is it always just me?

256
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:52,840
It's because the staff went overboard,
you know.

257
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:54,940
Is that the hotel over there?

258
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:56,040
Yes, that's the one.

259
00:12:56,630 --> 00:12:58,860
It's a pretty impressive hotel, isn't it?

260
00:13:02,380 --> 00:13:03,860
We have arrived.

261
00:13:06,300 --> 00:13:08,040
Where are you headed, sir?

262
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:12,640
I'm not going to be the one stuck with the short straw at the end!
I'm getting to the restaurant first!

263
00:13:13,140 --> 00:13:16,060
The buffet is actually at the
Garden Restaurant over here.

264
00:13:16,060 --> 00:13:17,020
What?!

265
00:13:25,420 --> 00:13:26,620
This way, please.

266
00:13:26,620 --> 00:13:28,400
Let me in too!

267
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:36,000
I'm terribly sorry,
but the garden is full here as well.

268
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:37,420
Do you love me or what!

269
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:40,760
We've prepared seating over there for you.

270
00:13:48,140 --> 00:13:49,020
Delicious!

271
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:55,320
How lovely.

272
00:13:55,320 --> 00:13:57,960
The food is delicious too,
so there's nothing to complain about.

273
00:13:57,960 --> 00:14:00,320
We really should be thankful to the senior officer,
shouldn't we.

274
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:01,260
Yeah, that's right.

275
00:14:01,260 --> 00:14:02,760
By the way, where's that guy?

276
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:03,700
And that gentleman?

277
00:14:11,180 --> 00:14:12,760
Why is it just me?

278
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:20,140
This will be your accommodation,
everyone.

279
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:22,360
Aren't we staying at that hotel?

280
00:14:23,140 --> 00:14:24,740
With that budget, that's far too many.

281
00:14:24,740 --> 00:14:27,340
But the inside is just like a hotel,
so don't worry.

282
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:29,720
As for the room assignments,

283
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:32,640
the ladies will each have
a cottage to themselves.

284
00:14:33,060 --> 00:14:35,980
And the other two cottages
will have two people each.

285
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:38,420
Wait, that leaves one person extra,
doesn't it?

286
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:41,740
I'm also here,
so there will be two left over.

287
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:44,240
Hold on!
So what are those two supposed to do?!

288
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:46,760
We've arranged for you on
the little island over there.

289
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:50,120
It's the optional Robinson Crusoe tour.

290
00:14:50,700 --> 00:14:51,720
Ooh.

291
00:14:51,740 --> 00:14:53,720
Well, Ryotsu can be one of them.

292
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:55,100
Why me?!

293
00:14:55,420 --> 00:14:56,844
Living on a remote island,

294
00:14:56,894 --> 00:14:59,440
it's perfect for someone as inhuman as you,
isn't it?

295
00:14:59,800 --> 00:15:00,540
Yeah, yeah.

296
00:15:01,140 --> 00:15:03,400
But what about the other person?

297
00:15:03,660 --> 00:15:05,560
Hey! I haven't said I'm going yet!

298
00:15:05,980 --> 00:15:08,000
Hey! Do something about the ceiling!

299
00:15:09,040 --> 00:15:11,600
Even if you say that,
this is the best I can do,

300
00:15:11,650 --> 00:15:13,340
after all, at 30,000 yen per person,

301
00:15:13,340 --> 00:15:14,140
Idiot!

302
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:15,840
30,000 yen?

303
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:19,980
Ryotsu, what do you mean by 30,000 yen?

304
00:15:20,160 --> 00:15:22,840
I believe the savings fund
should be 48,000 yen, though.

305
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:24,680
So you fudged it down to 30,000 yen.

306
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:26,760
You were planning to skim off the top,
weren't you?

307
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:28,754
Senpai, that's terrible,

308
00:15:28,804 --> 00:15:31,320
charging me 126,000 yen!

309
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:34,760
That's 186,000 yen in total.
You were going to pocket it all.

310
00:15:34,760 --> 00:15:37,740
That 180,000 is the amount
of your debt, Senpai.

311
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:40,820
High-low-V, indeed!

312
00:15:50,300 --> 00:15:53,560
You idiot!
You're getting exiled to an island!

313
00:15:57,820 --> 00:16:01,580
Why me?
I'm the one who's lost the most money...

314
00:16:01,580 --> 00:16:04,320
Can't be helped.
We lost at rock-paper-scissors.

315
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:12,200
Hey, can we really stay
on an island like this?

316
00:16:12,380 --> 00:16:14,660
Yes, please use this.

317
00:16:14,760 --> 00:16:15,200
What is it?

318
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:16,740
It's a hammock!

319
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:19,380
Well then,
we'll come pick you up tomorrow morning.

320
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:21,400
Hey, what about the bread and rice?
What about the food!

321
00:16:21,860 --> 00:16:23,380
Please find something suitable.

322
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:47,180
Nothing on this island

323
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:48,320
Yeah, you're right.

324
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:50,660
Well, since there's nothing to do,
let's just relax and sleep.

325
00:16:50,660 --> 00:16:51,920
Yeah, sounds good.

326
00:17:23,220 --> 00:17:27,540
Senpai, wake up! Senpai, again!

327
00:17:27,540 --> 00:17:31,540
Senpai, it's terrible!

328
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:33,900
What on earth is it?

329
00:17:33,900 --> 00:17:41,280
Why are you in the sea?

330
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:43,260
It must be high tide.

331
00:17:43,260 --> 00:17:47,480
So that's why it got dirtied, that bastard.

332
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:28,560
Anyway, saved for now.

333
00:18:28,560 --> 00:18:31,760
But Senior, you can't move at all, can you?

334
00:18:41,440 --> 00:18:42,480
Saved.

335
00:18:42,480 --> 00:18:46,060
What? Something weird just touched my...
stingy spot?

336
00:18:46,660 --> 00:18:47,700
Senior!

337
00:18:48,700 --> 00:19:10,860


338
00:19:10,860 --> 00:19:12,660
These are our bags, lucky!

339
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:14,700
One, two, heave!

340
00:19:18,810 --> 00:19:20,400
Could you be a little gentler?

341
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:20,720
Yes.

342
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:22,660
No, that's wrong.

343
00:19:23,420 --> 00:19:24,000
No, that's wrong.

344
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:25,020
No, that's wrong.

345
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:32,860
Cheers!

346
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:54,060
Next, how about a 4-night,
5-day Saipan trip for the whole family?

347
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:57,140
Those guys...

348
00:19:57,840 --> 00:19:59,520
What's wrong, senpai?

349
00:19:59,520 --> 00:20:02,320
Even though we're going through all this...

350
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:03,940
I won't forgive them.

351
00:20:06,340 --> 00:20:07,700
How about this one? Phuket.

352
00:20:07,700 --> 00:20:09,020
7 nights, 8 days.

353
00:20:09,020 --> 00:20:10,700
Wouldn't your wife be pleased too?

354
00:20:11,260 --> 00:20:12,040
Yeah, I suppose so.

355
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:14,740
It turned out to be a fun vacation trip,
didn't it?

356
00:20:15,700 --> 00:20:17,540
That's because we exiled
Ryo-tsu to the island.

357
00:20:17,540 --> 00:20:18,680
But it's a shame.

358
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:20,960
I wonder if Ryo-chan is
managing to get by out there.

359
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:21,980
Oh my.

360
00:20:23,160 --> 00:20:24,800
Wasn't that island, during the day...

361
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:27,300
It should have been bigger than that.

362
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:31,920
At high tide,
more than half of it goes under water.

363
00:20:33,180 --> 00:20:34,960
I wonder if the senior
officers are all right.

364
00:20:35,420 --> 00:20:37,420
If it's him, he'll probably be fine somehow.

365
00:20:37,420 --> 00:20:40,180
Surely they didn't tell
him anything about that?

366
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:43,040
Did I forget to mention it?

367
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:46,240
He threatened me over and over,
so it serves him right.

368
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:47,880
He should suffer a little.

369
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:49,220
Well, that's bad.

370
00:20:49,220 --> 00:20:53,440
He's bound to hold a grudge
against us and come back for revenge!

371
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:56,080
Over there, over there!

372
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:57,360
It's a signal fire!

373
00:20:58,420 --> 00:21:01,180
I'll kill him!

374
00:21:02,140 --> 00:21:03,240
I'll kill him!

375
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:05,380
This has turned into a real mess, hasn't it.

376
00:21:35,700 --> 00:21:36,400
It's an ambush!

377
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:38,320
We'll seize the stronghold!

378
00:21:48,980 --> 00:21:50,560
The enemy should still be asleep.

379
00:21:50,560 --> 00:21:51,180
Let's go!

380
00:21:51,180 --> 00:21:51,700
Yes!

381
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:54,780
It's a banana!

382
00:21:55,420 --> 00:21:56,380
Yaaah!

383
00:21:56,380 --> 00:21:58,380
We're in luck, senior.

384
00:21:58,380 --> 00:21:58,600
Yeah.

385
00:21:59,800 --> 00:22:01,380
It's corn!

386
00:22:01,970 --> 00:22:02,740
Yahoo!

387
00:22:02,740 --> 00:22:04,680
We're lucky, senpai.

388
00:22:04,680 --> 00:22:04,940
Yeah.

389
00:22:05,860 --> 00:22:07,320
It's Lonestar!

390
00:22:07,920 --> 00:22:08,760
Yahoo!

391
00:22:09,150 --> 00:22:09,720
Really, it is.

392
00:22:09,720 --> 00:22:11,060
Something's off, isn't it?

393
00:22:11,860 --> 00:22:12,680
Look.

394
00:22:13,360 --> 00:22:15,500
The cottage is getting
farther and farther away.

395
00:22:15,500 --> 00:22:16,660
You're right.

396
00:22:17,680 --> 00:22:18,580
This is a trap.

397
00:22:18,980 --> 00:22:19,320
A trap?

398
00:22:19,640 --> 00:22:21,400
It's the kind of tactic
the Chief would think up.

399
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:23,020
No way I'm falling for it.

400
00:22:23,020 --> 00:22:24,120
Now I'm going in.

401
00:22:25,740 --> 00:22:26,780
It's a 100-yen coin!

402
00:22:27,320 --> 00:22:28,980
Lucky, found a 100-yen coin!

403
00:22:30,940 --> 00:22:33,720
There are coins lying all over the place,
over there and over here!

404
00:22:34,340 --> 00:22:36,320
Super lucky, very very lucky!

405
00:22:36,320 --> 00:22:39,320
Senpai,
the money itself looks more like the trap.

406
00:22:39,660 --> 00:22:41,260
I don't care if it's a trap.

407
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:46,420
Motorcycle handlebars! Forks and a tank too!

408
00:22:46,560 --> 00:22:49,220
Super lucky! Super duper lucky! Yahoo!

409
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:51,400
More over here! Yahoo!

410
00:22:51,480 --> 00:22:53,500
Yahoo! Yahoo!

411
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:54,280
Yahoo!

412
00:22:55,100 --> 00:22:57,440
A ten-thousand-yen bill! And an engine!

413
00:22:57,720 --> 00:22:58,380
Yahoo!

414
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,380
He fell for it hook,
line, and sinker, Tsukun!

415
00:23:04,560 --> 00:23:05,140
Chief!

416
00:23:05,620 --> 00:23:07,720
Falling for such a simple trap!

417
00:23:07,820 --> 00:23:09,740
Yeah! We got him! Hand it over!

418
00:23:10,200 --> 00:23:13,640
Shut up! You're being forcibly
reassigned to the little island!

419
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:20,460
Tch! I'll make sure you
settle the accounts for this!

420
00:23:21,040 --> 00:23:22,620
You lot, you'd better remember this!

421
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:26,860
What an incorrigible guy.
But he's a bit pitiful, isn't he.

422
00:23:27,600 --> 00:23:29,516
Well, once he's cooled his head a little,

423
00:23:29,566 --> 00:23:31,860
we'll call him back at mealtime.

